WEBVTT

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:08.420
Why?

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.280
What happened?

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:15.320
The Chi-chan I knew was kind and strong, and...

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.960
You're just like back then.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.000
You haven't changed at all.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.810
Inside me, you see...

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.520
There's something I don't need.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.900
It's you, Suzu.

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:05.980
Friend / Bonds and Chains

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:11.060
You don't need me?

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:17.700
I've always treasured the 
memories I had with you.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.590
I've never forgotten them.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.410
There wasn't a day when I did.

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.040
They were a part of me.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.500
I'm the same way!

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:29.500
I've never forgotten!

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.280
Not for a moment after we said goodbye!

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.870
It's thanks to you that I've gotten this far!

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:38.930
Same here.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:40.700
Chi-chan!

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.930
I thought I had to be the person you admired.

00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:44.180
Every day.

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:45.220
Every day.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.120
Every day...

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.440
I tied myself down that way,

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.710
and I became weaker.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.600
Chi-chan...

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.280
But when I lost the Selector battle, I realized it.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.780
I only had one coin left...

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.910
Something slipped from my memories,

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.490
and I felt a sense of liberation 
I'd never felt before.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.790
Like the chains that had bound me were gone.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.300
So I thought that I was willing to lose.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.080
I was willing to relinquish my memories 
so my weak self could disappear.

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:20.550
But Satomi told me...

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.730
Sure, if you lose the battles, 
your LRIG will take over,

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:28.340
and you'll cease to be you.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.020
Is that true?

00:03:29.650 --> 00:03:30.480
Yeah.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:32.960
Chinatsu-chan...

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.730
There should be a more appropriate stage for you.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.190
Right?

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:44.530
If I win the Selector battles, 
I can control my memories.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.700
I can cut the chains that bind me.

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.290
I can live freely, the way I want to.

00:03:50.980 --> 00:03:53.030
So I'm going to get stronger.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:56.560
I'll win the Selector battles and be rid of you.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:57.440
Chi-chan—

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.120
That face again.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:00.010
I...

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.460
I love you, Chi-chan!

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:04.800
I always wanted to be you—

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.310
Shut up!

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:12.350
Don't use me for your own purposes anymore.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.440
Chi-chan!

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.230
Chi-chan!

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:15.850
You're pissing me off!

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:21.190
Welcome back, Suzu.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:23.960
Goodbye.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:37.960
Oh, dear...

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:51.260
<i>I didn't want to lose the memories we shared.</i>

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:55.230
Suzuko...

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:59.820
<i>But I was the only one who felt that way.</i>

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:04.130
<i>Chi-chan doesn't need them...</i>

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:05.840
<i>Is that true?</i>

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:19.340
The real me...

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.300
Oh, my... You're quite the
busybody today, aren't you?

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.690
Is it because of that rather aggressive girl?

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:33.040
You two are a bit alike, after all.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.700
People have their own reasons for fighting,

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:40.440
but you never know what 
life is going to bring!

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.400
Hey, w-wait...

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.090
Oh, Hanna? What's wrong?

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.090
B-Break.

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.840
I have writer's block.

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.680
I see!

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:14.140
Then I'll make you my special café au lait!

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.520
N-No.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:16.620
Halt.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.100
I'm going to bed for today.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.100
Okay, sure.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.300
Goodnight.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.620
<b>Study Hall</b>

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.250
Man, a proficiency test? That sucks.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.170
I'm gonna get killed...

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:42.790
If I don't pass the next one, 
they'll cut my allowance in half.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.480
That's going too far.

00:06:47.490 --> 00:06:48.670
Stupid.

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.400
Oh, wow! She's so cute!

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.570
I definitely prefer this one!

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:56.770
What about you, Shouhei?

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:00.460
You really do love soccer.

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:01.600
You're not joining the team?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:04.110
Oh, not anymore.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:07.330
This one's great, too!

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:08.360
Let me see.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.490
Check it out!

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:09.990
Shou-chan! Shou-chan!

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:11.510
There's a Selector nearby.

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.260
Morikawa...

00:07:16.010 --> 00:07:18.250
Come on, it doesn't have to be long.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:19.870
Shirai-kun?

00:07:20.940 --> 00:07:22.700
Did you need something from her?

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:24.790
Who are you?

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.210
He's a Selector.

00:07:24.790 --> 00:07:26.550
Think you're a hero or something?

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.010
Want to fight?

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:31.340
Hey, wait!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:34.220
<b>Peace Street</b>

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.860
What's with you?

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:51.100
I saved you, didn't I?

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:53.340
What are you talking about? I saved you!

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:55.550
Anyway, was it okay for you to be running?

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:56.350
Huh?

00:07:56.690 --> 00:07:58.400
I heard you got hurt a long time ago.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.860
Oh, I can't play soccer anymore,

00:08:01.860 --> 00:08:03.670
but I can run a little.

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:06.140
You're a Selector, aren't you?

00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:08.420
You are too, right?

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:13.300
Want to do it with me?

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.510
I'm fine with doing it.

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:19.740
I don't fight battles.

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.160
You don't?

00:08:21.160 --> 00:08:22.520
There's a time limit.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:23.140
I know.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:24.900
Then why not?

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.270
I did it once.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:27.560
But...

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.060
Phosphorescent Samsara.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.950
Then I'll use Pinch Defense 
to cancel your attack!

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:36.530
Good choice.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:41.140
Okay! Summon Apparition Nurari!

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.660
Attack!

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.480
All right!

00:08:46.480 --> 00:08:47.790
Shou-chan! Shou-chan!

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.860
Battles feel so good, don't they?

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:51.800
Yeah!

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.720
As good as soccer?

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:56.440
It feels great to win, doesn't it?

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:58.480
Thanks.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:00.670
I'm glad I could fight with you.

00:09:00.670 --> 00:09:02.350
You're glad?

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.200
Does it make you that happy to win?

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:07.440
Thanks to you, I'm done for!

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:09.640
I...

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:11.000
I don't want to disappear.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:14.440
I don't want to disappear. 
I don't want to disappear.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:17.740
I don't want to disappear. 
I don't want to disappear.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:20.990
I don't want to disappear. 
I don't want to disappear.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:24.760
I don't want to disappear. 
I don't want to disappear.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:26.420
I don't want to disappear...

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:28.430
I don't want to disappear.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:29.930
I'm better off not fighting those battles.

00:09:28.430 --> 00:09:29.930
I don't want to disappear...

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:35.550
I don't want to win if it means 
hurting other people.

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:42.760
And if I still have any coins 
after ninety days, I win.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:43.620
You win?

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:44.450
Yeah.

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:47.420
I'll lose some of my memories, though.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:48.680
Does that...

00:09:48.680 --> 00:09:52.360
We got into an argument about 
whether he should fight or not.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:57.270
I let things kinda get out of hand, 
and I told him about that...

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:59.910
And he stopped wanting to fight at all!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.400
Stay out of this!

00:10:02.870 --> 00:10:04.900
But are you all right with that?

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:08.760
You can't choose the memories 
you want to save, right?

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.640
It's better than fighting battles.

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:15.400
Besides, remember what you said?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:19.010
He got hurt before the tournament?

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:20.360
That sucks.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.220
What about the scholarship he was getting?

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:23.890
It ain't happening now.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.450
Poor guy...

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:42.880
Morikawa?

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.540
I practiced too much and injured it.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:50.620
I brought this upon myself.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:51.250
I see.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:55.180
From now on, I'll forget about soccer 
and enjoy lots of different things.

00:10:56.480 --> 00:10:58.540
Why don't you join me?

00:10:58.540 --> 00:11:02.220
Can you just forget it so easily?

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:06.970
I think forgetting is wrong.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:09.120
Even if you can't play soccer,

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.220
the way you tried so hard, 
the emotions you felt...

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:14.290
They're important to you.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:18.660
See you. And cheer up.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:25.030
The words you said to me that day saved me.

00:11:26.800 --> 00:11:30.840
So I don't want to lie to myself 
during these battles.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:32.390
I see.

00:11:32.950 --> 00:11:33.920
Well, um...

00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:37.100
All of my memories with you are important.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:39.090
You might not remember it,

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:44.010
but maybe we could change the memory 
of when you turned me down,

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.440
and hang out and have fun together...

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:48.380
I'm sorry.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:52.050
There's something I don't need.

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:53.690
Something you don't need?

00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:57.900
That's why I'm betting everything on this fight.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:01.650
I'll win the battles and be rid of what binds me.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:09.620
The me you knew wasn't really me.

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:12.680
She rejected you again, Shou-chan!

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.460
You got rejected!

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:16.710
Shut up!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:28.640
<b>Homura Suzuko 
Were Friends (Unknown) 
Morikawa Chinatsu (Too Soon)</b>

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:26.970
<b>Mikage Hanna</b>

00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:31.970
Hi, it's Satomi.

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:34.980
Yes, I was thinking it was time.

00:12:35.550 --> 00:12:39.230
Yeah, got it. Leave it to me.

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.070
I'll set you up with the perfect battle.

00:12:43.790 --> 00:12:44.590
Well?

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.320
Who do you want to fight?

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:00.160
Inside me, you see...

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.300
There's something I don't need.

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:05.760
I'll win the Selector battles and be rid of you.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.430
She says I'm no good now.

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:18.280
What am I supposed to do?

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:20.610
Fight the battles.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:28.660
Suzuko-san?

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.280
I wanted to talk to you about something.

00:13:34.130 --> 00:13:35.250
Roger.

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:40.510
Go ahead.

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:42.440
Oh, um...

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:45.760
I wanted your opinion, Hanna-chan.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:51.720
It just doesn't seem to me like 
that's what Chi-chan really thinks.

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:53.610
Doubt.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.690
What do you mean by "really"?

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:03.670
And is the answer she gave actually that bad?

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:05.740
Sympathy.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:10.950
Isn't it a good thing to realize 
who you truly are?

00:14:11.840 --> 00:14:14.520
If someone decides they don't need friendship,

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:17.800
we should respect their decision.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:19.670
But...

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:23.760
I can't just ignore her. We're friends.

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.330
Friends...

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.270
Confirmation. Go ahead.

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:34.510
This is for a battle...

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:37.520
It has to be some mistake, right?

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.020
You remember the contract, don't you?

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.850
Once you're entered, 
you can't turn down battles.

00:14:43.860 --> 00:14:45.220
No...

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:50.450
<b>Sender: Satomi-san 
To: Suzuko 

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:02.650
I'm back.

00:15:03.350 --> 00:15:04.730
Welcome home.

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:06.230
You're early.

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.860
Did you finish your shift?

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:08.770
Yeah.

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:11.360
Dad, you're home early, too?

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:12.480
Yeah.

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:15.610
Chinatsu, we need to talk.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:17.150
What is it?

00:15:17.150 --> 00:15:18.270
Honey...

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:20.770
Y-Yeah.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.820
Chinatsu, about going to college...

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.210
I hate to tell you this, but...

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:27.400
I'm not giving up.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:31.490
Chinatsu, we're not saying you can't go.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:32.320
Just a different school—

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:33.820
I'm not giving up.

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.080
Never.

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:38.620
Chinatsu? Wait, Chinatsu!

00:15:51.620 --> 00:15:53.020
Hanna-chan...

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:54.210
Demand.

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.570
If there's something you want to take back,

00:15:56.570 --> 00:15:58.440
fight for real, please.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.840
But I can't fight you!

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:01.800
Reasonable.

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:04.020
You and I are both Selectors.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:08.170
We must use the battles to get what we want.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:11.460
Addition.

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:16.030
The other reason is my simple 
interest in battling you.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:17.740
Hanna-chan...

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:18.720
Suzuko,

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.830
why do you fight?

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:24.140
Why?

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:25.870
For Chi-chan—

00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:27.040
Warning.

00:16:27.660 --> 00:16:29.720
Don't underestimate this.

00:16:30.540 --> 00:16:33.170
These battles aren't fought for others.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.230
They're fought for oneself.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.740
<i>I won't lose...</i>

00:16:53.600 --> 00:16:56.630
<i>I won't let this beat me.</i>

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:03.120
<i>I'll fight and get what I want on my own.</i>

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.660
Spread Death.

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:14.670
Riru, grow!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:17.540
Summon Garnet Star!

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:20.800
Banish her center...

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:22.390
And attack!

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:37.390
Unexpected.

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:40.220
To use such a card in a Valor deck?

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.830
But power is just a vessel.

00:17:43.830 --> 00:17:45.960
Without a strong will, it's meaningless.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:48.700
I'm different!

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:53.040
Grow, and coin bet!

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:54.810
Blind.

00:17:57.980 --> 00:18:00.340
I can't see anything.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:01.660
Turn end.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:05.640
Now, what will you do?

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:08.420
<i>Attack? Defend?</i>

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:09.420
<i>Which?</i>

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:10.370
Suzuko...

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:11.730
Your coin.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:14.440
Yeah.

00:18:21.400 --> 00:18:22.740
Coin bet!

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:26.580
Honest!

00:18:29.250 --> 00:18:30.190
What's this?

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:32.650
Sparkly!

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:35.260
Looks like she used her coin.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.590
Hanna-chan!

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:40.150
Are there any traps hidden in your cards?

00:18:40.760 --> 00:18:46.770
Oh? You're not just going to tell 
her, are you, Hanna-sama?

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:49.480
<i>Understanding.</i>

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:52.150
<i>The answer is overlaid on the spoken words,</i>

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:54.900
<i>and you can't avoid answering.</i>

00:18:57.720 --> 00:18:58.790
Correct.

00:18:59.440 --> 00:19:01.840
I am hiding traps.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.120
I have a method of counterattack.

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:05.450
Suzuko!

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.680
Yeah, I'll pass.

00:19:07.680 --> 00:19:08.840
Turn end.

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:17.920
No traps?

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:20.840
Attacking would've been the right move?

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.180
Laughter.

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:24.300
I didn't lie.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:26.800
Insufficient thought.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:30.050
You never asked where my traps were.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:31.480
You can't...

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:32.920
Certainty.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:34.340
I win!

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:36.160
Attack with two Oigona!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.080
Riru!

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:52.920
Riru...

00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:58.120
What do I do, Riru?

00:19:58.120 --> 00:19:59.140
Weakness.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:01.840
First Chinatsu-san, then Riru-san?

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:04.140
Advice.

00:20:04.670 --> 00:20:08.010
You, the Selector, are the one fighting.

00:20:08.970 --> 00:20:13.020
Do you intend to keep averting 
your eyes from that fact?

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:18.230
Suzuko, your next command...

00:20:18.870 --> 00:20:20.210
Turn end.

00:20:20.210 --> 00:20:21.380
Suzuko!

00:20:21.840 --> 00:20:22.740
Conclusion.

00:20:23.360 --> 00:20:25.080
We are Selectors.

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:29.080
At all times, there are only winners and losers.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.330
Ancient Gate!

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:41.030
You haven't changed at all.

00:20:42.000 --> 00:20:45.340
Don't use me for your own purposes anymore.

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:49.310
Goodbye.

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:56.350
Just one more.

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.370
Why?

00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:16.800
Why do I have to fight these battles?

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:23.700
Why?

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:26.170
Just prove it.

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:29.400
If you think you are correct...

00:21:30.520 --> 00:21:33.390
If you really don't want to lose...

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:35.930
Then use me.

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:37.260
Riru?

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:40.730
Hello?

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:44.990
Yes, let me take that job.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:55.420
<i>I won't lose.</i>

00:23:26.390 --> 00:23:28.980
Shall I introduce you to the bookmaker?

00:23:28.500 --> 00:23:29.720
Can you really give it up?

00:23:29.720 --> 00:23:30.890
Now, let's battle.

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:31.550
You can't run away.

00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.630
If you lose this fight, you'll disappear.

00:23:33.510 --> 00:23:34.470
Attack!

00:23:34.260 --> 00:23:36.370
Disappear! Never let me see you again!

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:37.580
If I disappear...

00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:41.020
Battle / Past and Present

00:23:38.110 --> 00:23:41.020
Next time: Battle / Past and Present.
